fact template_fact {
  title    = "Template — fact"
  audience = :both
  related  = [fact, unit_decision_guide]
  body {
    p "A **fact** is a container of values: a default, a limit, a lookup table, a version matrix, an option list, a glossary. The test is that nobody argues with it — you would cite it, not explain it. A fact whose body is mostly prose is usually a concept in disguise."

    h2 "Skeleton"
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
// data/fact/<id>.wcl — then add `import "./<id>.wcl"` to data/fact/main.wcl
fact <id> {
  title    = "<What the values are>"
  audience = :both
  related  = [<up to ~5 ids>]

  body {
    p "<One sentence of context: what these values are and when they apply.>"

    table {
      header = ["<Column>", "<Column>"]
      rows = [
        ["<value>", "<meaning>"],
      ]
    }

    code "<lang>" { source = <<'EXAMPLE'
<the values in use, if a sample helps>
EXAMPLE
    }
  }
}
SRC
    }

    h2 "Fields"
    table {
      header = ["Field", "What goes in it"]
      rows = [
        ["`title`", "Names the values, not the topic — \"Default ports\", \"Escape sequences\", \"Exit codes\""],
        ["`related`", "The concept the values belong to, and little else"],
        ["`body`", "Lead with one sentence of context, then the table. A fact with no table or code block is rare and probably misfiled"],
      ]
    }
    p "There is no `summary` field on a fact: the `title` carries it, so make the title specific enough to stand alone in an index."

    h2 "Filled example"
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
fact exit_codes {
  title    = "Exit codes"
  audience = :both
  related  = [validate_format]

  body {
    p "`wcl check` distinguishes the two failure modes by exit code, so a script can tell a broken file from a schema violation."
    table {
      header = ["Code", "Meaning"]
      rows = [
        ["`0`", "Valid"],
        ["`1`", "Parse error — the file is not WCL"],
        ["`2`", "Schema violation — the file parses but breaks its @document"],
      ]
    }
  }
}
SRC
    }

    h2 "Done when"
    list {
      li "The values are the content; the prose is one sentence of context."
      li "Every row is checkable against the thing it documents."
      li "The title is specific enough to be an index row on its own."
      li "It is pinned into an `index`."
    }
  }
}
